			<div class="content" id="post-content-1476892">
									

<blockquote>
<p>A team of two secure communications personnel fluent in German are to monitor SCP-1142 at all times. In case of verified contact,</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Since the thing only it has a receiver, it would make more sense for the signal to be recorded automatically, and for someone fluent in German to check daily to see if anything was recorded. And &quot;contact&quot; implies two-way communication, which can't be done with just a receiver.</p>
<p>If, on the other hand, the SCP was a receiver <em>and</em> a transmitter, but all attempts to speak to SCP-1142-1 have failed so far, it would make sense to keep a German speaker around at all hours of the day, since the next time they receive a transmission they'll want to try talking back <em>again</em>, in case the next time talking back works.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Analysis of transmissions recorded by authorized personnel have yielded several critical points of divergence from our timeline.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I don't think &quot;authorized&quot; is needed here.</p>

